WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.953
- All right.

00:00:00.953 --> 00:00:02.400
Well, before we end our season premiere,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.680
I wanna share one of the
most incredible stories

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:05.513
of the summer.

00:00:05.513 --> 00:00:06.934
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:09.270
(lively upbeat music)

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.070
We all saw the devastating images

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.990
out of Eastern Kentucky this summer.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.780
Thousands lost their
homes to historic flooding

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.060
with many clinging to their rooftops.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.040
I've been through
Kentucky many, many times.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.270
These are some of the best people.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.380
So, it's no surprise that there were

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.970
countless heroes involved.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:27.570
But, I wanna talk about one
in particular, Nathan Day,

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:30.570
a former coal miner, waded
into the rising water

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.650
and helped save nine people,
including five children.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:35.483
And get this,

00:00:35.483 --> 00:00:38.580
two of the nine were his
former school teachers.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.660
We have Nathan joining us now
along with his wife, Krystal.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.010
Thank y'all for joining us.

00:00:44.881 --> 00:00:45.840
- Thank you for having us.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.100
- Yeah, so, this is a
really important detail.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.230
So, it was pitch black out,

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.730
nobody could see anything, right?

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.450
- No, probably scariest thing
I've ever done in my life.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:58.320
- Yeah, I can't imagine.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.480
Pitch black and wading through
water, you have no idea

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.010
how fast it's going, what's in it.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.140
- Well, when I heard those kids screaming,

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.060
you know, I went to 'em.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.750
- But during this time,
what he wasn't seeing

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.050
that I could see, was as he was getting

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.450
the children and the moms off the roof,

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.660
there was

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:18.990
cars.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:22.680
What was like a little
small creek, it's a river,

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.500
a raging river now, and
there's cars going down

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.470
that's going, you know,
at least 50 miles an hour,

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:29.880
crashing into everything.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.320
- That's what I'm saying, you have no idea

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.160
and it's black out, yeah.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.900
- [Nick] Well, you couldn't
see the houses either.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.930
- There was a lot of dangerous
stuff out there that, I mean,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.790
we both could have been killed in.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.623
But, could you live with yourself?

00:01:41.623 --> 00:01:42.657
- And hearing those
screams and not helping.

00:01:42.657 --> 00:01:44.670
- [Krystal] And hearing
children screaming.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.410
- I'm just glad there's life.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.633
You know, I'm just glad there's life.

00:01:47.633 --> 00:01:48.466
(audience clapping)

00:01:48.466 --> 00:01:49.547
- What a beautiful thing, though.

00:01:49.547 --> 00:01:51.690
It wasn't just, y'all had the community,

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.670
you do find out the community you live in.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.950
And I'm from a small town, so I get that.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.570
You, you know, community,
you wrap yourself,

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.370
somebody needs help, you help them.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.203
- [Nick] Unbelievable.

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:01.036
- You know, and I think that's incredible.

00:02:01.036 --> 00:02:02.970
- [Nick] Our community
has been unbelievable.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.320
- [Kelly] Hope is powerful.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.460
Well, thank you so much for
being here, and thank you

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.260
for just being you and
having the hearts you have.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.870
And thank you so much for your
accent, 'cause it's amazing.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:13.703
And I love your accent so much.

00:02:13.703 --> 00:02:14.536
- Oh Kelly, you are welcome.

00:02:14.536 --> 00:02:17.070
I'm like, I could listen
to you talk all day long.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.240
- Call me, we'll talk away.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.891
- [Kelly] I'm liking
y'all's post right now.

00:02:20.891 --> 00:02:21.840
(bell dings)

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.490
And that's not all,
our season long partner

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.080
Pilot Pen, makers of friction,

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.000
the go-to erasable pen of
The Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.910
want to celebrate those acting fearlessly,

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:30.990
obviously just like you.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:33.358
So, they're giving you a thousand dollars.

00:02:33.358 --> 00:02:34.191
(audience clapping)

00:02:34.191 --> 00:02:35.343
And there's more.

00:02:36.372 --> 00:02:38.580
I know there's a lot of
rebuilding that needs to happen

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.440
in Nathan and Krystal's community.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.537
So, we are giving the eastern
Kentucky flood relief fund

00:02:43.537 --> 00:02:44.680
$20,000.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.551
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:02:47.551 --> 00:02:50.100
And we're also encouraging
everyone at home

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.130
to make their own donation
to help relief efforts.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.020
Visit our Insta Story to find out how.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.730
You know, if you got, even
if it's a little bit of cash,

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.920
it doesn't have to be $20,000,
doesn't have to be $1000.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.653
Anything you can donate
makes a big difference.

